# Run the way strip-smoke.yml runs it: strip applied inside a git checkout,
# so `tool/check_epic_coverage.dart` (which reads `git ls-files`) still sees
# the index entries for the deleted sample paths, exactly as CI does. Run in
# a plain rsync'd copy with no `.git`, that check reports
# `Bad state: listing tracked files failed (exit 128)` - an artefact of the
# reproduction, not of this change.
